{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536285-age-alteration","id":1536285,"title":"Age Alteration","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-05-25T23:41:18-07:00","id":1536285,"title":"Age Alteration","content":"Does anyone know how the mechanics for magic that alters age are supposed to work? I know that in 2e it requires Life 3 and Time 3, but I was not able to find details on how such magic actually functioned. Based on the text, it seems like the idea is that the mage decides on a specific age beforehand, and a success indicates that the alteration is successfully conducted. Also, the text does not specify if the physical attributes of the target are affected by the change in age. I am guessing that additional magic is required to adjust the physical attributes of the target, so presumably an individual who was rendered an old man by the spell would not actually suffer a reduction in physical capabilities. Does anyone know how magic of this sort is supposed to work?<br /> <br /> I am also interested in what people think about the Arcana that are used for this kind of magic. I remember that in 1e, age alteration required Life 4. In a way, age alteration magic is both more easy and more difficult to access in 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-26T03:19:56-07:00","id":1536288,"title":"","content":"Depends on what you mean by age alteration. In 2e Time can do it on its own with Temporal Summoning (weaving) but this isn't lasting.<br /> <br /> Life is also able to do it, with Accelerate Growth as an example, Transform Life might also be used creatively to give some deaging process which several animals appear to have, but I think taking an elderly person to the health of a 25 year old would be perfecting...<br /> <br /> You could also compare with Regeneration... I am pretty sure none of these are Lasting, as per the section on Liches.<br /> <br /> Death may also be an option, fraying the Decay that causes aging or the reverse, but it seems more blunt a tool.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-26T05:44:49-07:00","id":1536292,"title":"","content":"I would note that the Many Faces spell already contains parameters for rearranging the target's Physical Attribute dots in a manner consistent with the new body that the subject is given. I'm going to suppose that it can't actually increase them, regardless of the apparent physical qualities of the new body, because it's outside of the spell's Practice.<br /> <br /> So you probably can end up with a situation of turning an elderly person into a younger one, and while they may well have a number of ancillary benefits (if they had arthritis, that clears up), it doesn't quite restore their original strength without it being at the expense of something else.<br /> <br /> If one wants to make it thorough, it's probably a good idea to make it a combined spell with Honing the Form.<br /> <br /> The Arcana thing is simply a function of how the Edition is making the Practices a lot more consistent as the basis for how spells work, without regard for the supposed relevance of the end result. Outright mind control up to the level of making a person do something suicidal is 2 dots because it's a Ruling effect. Turning fungi into insects is 4 dots because regardless of how insignificant one thinks either of those life forms are, it's a transformation to the most thorough extent, and that means Patterning.<br /> <br /> I would also note that Many Faces probably isn't a great choice to revert one's life span continuously, because even if the spell is Indefinite, you're eventually going to age back up again, and then your only way to wind it back again is to cast the same spell with a higher Potency to overwrite the currently active one. You're eventually going to hit a point where the Potency gets higher than you might effectively be able to exceed with the next spell. And you can't just drop the spell to start off with a fresh one at low Potency, because then you'll turn back into your real age.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 05-26-2024, 09:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-28T12:11:55-07:00","id":1536452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536285-age-alteration?p=1536288#post1536288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends on what you mean by age alteration. In 2e Time can do it on its own with Temporal Summoning (weaving) but this isn't lasting.<br /> <br /> Life is also able to do it, with Accelerate Growth as an example, Transform Life might also be used creatively to give some deaging process which several animals appear to have, but I think taking an elderly person to the health of a 25 year old would be perfecting...<br /> <br /> You could also compare with Regeneration... I am pretty sure none of these are Lasting, as per the section on Liches.<br /> <br /> Death may also be an option, fraying the Decay that causes aging or the reverse, but it seems more blunt a tool.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had not been aware that Time was also able to accomplish that effect on its own. I remember that Time effects could be used to establish a personal temporal stasis, but I am fairly sure that the duration of such spells was not Lasting. The idea of using Life to give individuals the capability of some animals to return previous life stages is interesting, but I think that that would probably trigger at a specific age and it might not be very convenient. It still sounds cool though. I can see how returning the old to young adulthood could involve Perfecting, though I also wonder if that would just give them vigor without changing age or extending their lifespan. Granted, such spells would not really be useful for extending the lifespan much anyway, given how they are generally not Lasting. Thank you for your input, in any case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-28T12:19:18-07:00","id":1536454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536285-age-alteration?p=1536292#post1536292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would note that the Many Faces spell already contains parameters for rearranging the target's Physical Attribute dots in a manner consistent with the new body that the subject is given. I'm going to suppose that it can't actually increase them, regardless of the apparent physical qualities of the new body, because it's outside of the spell's Practice.<br /> <br /> So you probably can end up with a situation of turning an elderly person into a younger one, and while they may well have a number of ancillary benefits (if they had arthritis, that clears up), it doesn't quite restore their original strength without it being at the expense of something else.<br /> <br /> If one wants to make it thorough, it's probably a good idea to make it a combined spell with Honing the Form.<br /> <br /> The Arcana thing is simply a function of how the Edition is making the Practices a lot more consistent as the basis for how spells work, without regard for the supposed relevance of the end result. Outright mind control up to the level of making a person do something suicidal is 2 dots because it's a Ruling effect. Turning fungi into insects is 4 dots because regardless of how insignificant one thinks either of those life forms are, it's a transformation to the most thorough extent, and that means Patterning.<br /> <br /> I would also note that Many Faces probably isn't a great choice to revert one's life span continuously, because even if the spell is Indefinite, you're eventually going to age back up again, and then your only way to wind it back again is to cast the same spell with a higher Potency to overwrite the currently active one. You're eventually going to hit a point where the Potency gets higher than you might effectively be able to exceed with the next spell. And you can't just drop the spell to start off with a fresh one at low Potency, because then you'll turn back into your real age.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had not known that Many Faces already allowed for Physical Attribute dots to be reallocated, actually. That could be used to add to their vigor to some extent, albeit at the expense of other capabilities, as you mentioned. As you said, I think that such a spell would really be best when combined with Honing the Form. <br /> <br /> You are right in that Many Faces and similar types of magic are not very effective at actually extending the lifespan, but it seems like it would still be useful for the purposes of disguises. Appearing like an old man, for example, could be useful for avoiding notice. In fact, by the way that Many Faces functions, it seems like one's Physical Attributes would not actually be adversely affected in such a scenario.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-30T01:03:12-07:00","id":1536554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verlan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536285-age-alteration#post1536285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone know how the mechanics for magic that alters age are supposed to work? I know that in 2e it requires Life 3 and Time 3, but I was not able to find details on how such magic actually functioned. Based on the text, it seems like the idea is that the mage decides on a specific age beforehand, and a success indicates that the alteration is successfully conducted. Also, the text does not specify if the physical attributes of the target are affected by the change in age. I am guessing that additional magic is required to adjust the physical attributes of the target, so presumably an individual who was rendered an old man by the spell would not actually suffer a reduction in physical capabilities. Does anyone know how magic of this sort is supposed to work?<br /> <br /> I am also interested in what people think about the Arcana that are used for this kind of magic. I remember that in 1e, age alteration required Life 4. In a way, age alteration magic is both more easy and more difficult to access in 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say <i>reverting age back</i> is Life Perfecting or Death Fraying. Time Weaving could probably rewind personal clock back (as per Temporal Summoning). In case you want to live (almost) forever, your best option would be getting a Life or Death Shielding spell stopping aging, like Veil of Moments, but without it's downsides, and then casting it with Indefinite Duration while safely relinquishing it. In case it is dispelled, just cast it again. This would prolong your lifespan long enough that instead of dying to an old age, dying to Mysteries would be your main concern. As for reverting age back <i>permanently</i> - I would allow it on Regeneration with +2 Reach option. Yeah, I know that corebook Regeneration does not have that, but I see it as cheap drama forcing you to look for ways around it, such as Weaving regeneration abilities from lizards or hydras and then waiting for them to grow your parts of the body back. Ultimately, as always, Storyteller decides what is possible and what isn't on his table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-30T12:21:40-07:00","id":1536574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536285-age-alteration?p=1536554#post1536554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would say <i>reverting age back</i> is Life Perfecting or Death Fraying. Time Weaving could probably rewind personal clock back (as per Temporal Summoning). In case you want to live (almost) forever, your best option would be getting a Life or Death Shielding spell stopping aging, like Veil of Moments, but without it's downsides, and then casting it with Indefinite Duration while safely relinquishing it. In case it is dispelled, just cast it again. This would prolong your lifespan long enough that instead of dying to an old age, dying to Mysteries would be your main concern. As for reverting age back <i>permanently</i> - I would allow it on Regeneration with +2 Reach option. Yeah, I know that corebook Regeneration does not have that, but I see it as cheap drama forcing you to look for ways around it, such as Weaving regeneration abilities from lizards or hydras and then waiting for them to grow your parts of the body back. Ultimately, as always, Storyteller decides what is possible and what isn't on his table.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see why Life Perfecting or Death Fraying would be used to actually render oneself younger. As you said, if you just want to live longer, it seems like a spell preventing the aging process from occurring would be more effective. Personally, I was not as interested in using magic for life extension as I was for using magic for disguises. I was just sort of curious as to how that would work mechanically. I am guessing that such magic could not really be Lasting, as it could then be used for life extension. I am interested by your suggestion in regards to Regeneration, though. I usually think of physical damage when thinking about Regeneration, so I had not considered how it might affect the aging process. I like the idea of applying the regenerative capabilities of certain animals to oneself through the use of magic, as you and another in the thread have suggested.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-30T14:34:42-07:00","id":1536586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verlan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536285-age-alteration?p=1536574#post1536574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I usually think of physical damage when thinking about Regeneration, so I had not considered how it might affect the aging process.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really think it works, when the spell is specifically described in terms of restoring tissues and bodily functions that are lost or originally absent. I can see Regeneration fixing a trait or feature that one has lost to aging, but the end result will be a healthier example of a person at the same age rather than reversing aging altogether.<br /> <br /> This is all in recognition of the fact that aging as a biological mechanism is actually kind of weird and still not well understood. Despite a lot of study, biologists still don't really have a great grasp of exactly why animal bodies change over time as they do, and ultimately break down.<br /> <br /> This is not to say that Awakened magic shouldn't be able to affect the matter due to lack of scientific understanding, just that conceiving of aging as a form of damage that can be reversed in the same way as a severed limb is a bit crude.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verlan</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea of applying the regenerative capabilities of certain animals to oneself through the use of magic, as you and another in the thread have suggested.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whereas this is something that I unreservedly dislike. As far as I'm concerned, it's one thing to follow the rule that creative applications of the Arcana can arrive at conclusions other than the ones presented in the book, and quite something else that trivially renders a suggested spell, and all of its dramatic conceits, completely obsolete.<br /> <br /> A person might regard that drama as &quot;cheap&quot; in the first place, but I place a bit more respect in the motivations of the writers who put it there to begin with.<br /> <br /> That's not to say that I'd rule granting oneself reptilian or amphibian regeneration to be off the table entirely, just that the results may be a bit different to (and maybe somewhat inferior) what could be granted with a high level of Awakened magic.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-30T20:07:03-07:00","id":1536600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536285-age-alteration?p=1536586#post1536586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not to say that I'd rule granting oneself reptilian or amphibian regeneration to be off the table entirely,</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they were talking about <b><i>Turritopsis dohrnii</i></b>, the Cnidarian known as the immortal jellyfish, who can phase from adult back to polip <i>ad \u00e6ternum</i>, though I think this would be less immortality and more reincarnation through self-gestation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-31T05:06:04-07:00","id":1536616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536285-age-alteration?p=1536600#post1536600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think they were talking about <b><i>Turritopsis dohrnii</i></b>, the Cnidarian known as the immortal jellyfish, who can phase from adult back to polip <i>ad \u00e6ternum</i>, though I think this would be less immortality and more reincarnation through self-gestation.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds like the capstone attainment of a reincarnation legacy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-31T13:26:24-07:00","id":1536635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536285-age-alteration?p=1536600#post1536600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think they were talking about <b><i>Turritopsis dohrnii</i></b>, the Cnidarian known as the immortal jellyfish, who can phase from adult back to polip <i>ad \u00e6ternum</i>, though I think this would be less immortality and more reincarnation through self-gestation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the conditions for regarding a continuity of selfhood might be a bit different between a human being and something that literally doesn't even have a brain.<br /> <br /> Like, maybe a mage could bestow upon themselves a capability to break down into a polyp at old age which buds off into several identically cloned... what, foetuses? Newborn humans? Some other form that will be a bit hard pressed for early survival barring some way to secure care.<br /> <br /> The transitions of the soul remain one of the deepest mysteries, but I feel confident in saying that there's a point somewhere in that transition where you end up as actually dead and it goes on its way. The clones might get new souls through the usual mechanisms*, and maybe a person could even secure a means of ensuring that an exact copy of their consciousness, but I don't think their Awakening is going to carry over.<br /> <br /> * Although maybe not, considering that most other forms of magically creating people seem to be outside of that process.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536285-age-alteration?p=1536616#post1536616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That sounds like the capstone attainment of a reincarnation legacy.</div> </div> </div> </div>What spell would it be modelled off of?<br /> <br /> For that matter, what would the rest of the Attainments do?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-31T15:01:30-07:00","id":1536648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536285-age-alteration?p=1536586#post1536586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't really think it works, when the spell is specifically described in terms of restoring tissues and bodily functions that are lost or originally absent. I can see Regeneration fixing a trait or feature that one has lost to aging, but the end result will be a healthier example of a person at the same age rather than reversing aging altogether.<br /> <br /> This is all in recognition of the fact that aging as a biological mechanism is actually kind of weird and still not well understood. Despite a lot of study, biologists still don't really have a great grasp of exactly why animal bodies change over time as they do, and ultimately break down.<br /> <br /> This is not to say that Awakened magic shouldn't be able to affect the matter due to lack of scientific understanding, just that conceiving of aging as a form of damage that can be reversed in the same way as a severed limb is a bit crude.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Whereas this is something that I unreservedly dislike. As far as I'm concerned, it's one thing to follow the rule that creative applications of the Arcana can arrive at conclusions other than the ones presented in the book, and quite something else that trivially renders a suggested spell, and all of its dramatic conceits, completely obsolete.<br /> <br /> A person might regard that drama as &quot;cheap&quot; in the first place, but I place a bit more respect in the motivations of the writers who put it there to begin with.<br /> <br /> That's not to say that I'd rule granting oneself reptilian or amphibian regeneration to be off the table entirely, just that the results may be a bit different to (and maybe somewhat inferior) what could be granted with a high level of Awakened magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are some fair points. I meant damage in a more general way; Regeneration is distinct from healing. In particular, I think that cellular decay came to mind, but that is a bit of an odd situation as the process is natural. It reminded me of how telomere shortening is biologically programmed. Arguably, Regeneration could not effectively alleviate the frailties of age, as such frailties are due to the body's normal functioning. <br /> <br /> As for utilizing the traits of animals, I think that that could be used for flavor more than anything else. You could still have the normal Arcana requirements, but have the acquisition of animal characteristics be the mechanism by which the effect is achieved. Also, I think that you would probably have to use a trait that explicitly involves extending the lifespan. The example of the jellyfish species that can revert to a juvenile state comes to mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-31T15:12:28-07:00","id":1536649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536285-age-alteration?p=1536635#post1536635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the conditions for regarding a continuity of selfhood might be a bit different between a human being and something that literally doesn't even have a brain.<br /> <br /> Like, maybe a mage could bestow upon themselves a capability to break down into a polyp at old age which buds off into several identically cloned... what, foetuses? Newborn humans? Some other form that will be a bit hard pressed for early survival barring some way to secure care.<br /> <br /> The transitions of the soul remain one of the deepest mysteries, but I feel confident in saying that there's a point somewhere in that transition where you end up as actually dead and it goes on its way. The clones might get new souls through the usual mechanisms*, and maybe a person could even secure a means of ensuring that an exact copy of their consciousness, but I don't think their Awakening is going to carry over.<br /> <br /> * Although maybe not, considering that most other forms of magically creating people seem to be outside of that process.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> What spell would it be modelled off of?<br /> <br /> For that matter, what would the rest of the Attainments do?</div> </div> </div> </div>In order to ensure continuity of consciousness, it seems like some form of possession would be necessary. I am guessing that Mind and Death would likely need to be involved. Assuming that the soul of the mage is unable to inhabit the body in question, though, I still think that that body would be inhabited by another soul, as seen in the normal process of incarnation. While such magic could not extend the lifespan of an individual, it could still have other utilities. If the person wants to preserve their genetic profile in the physical world, then such magic could be of use. If the memories of the mage were transferred, then critical information could be preserved. I kind of wonder if that might degrade Wisdom, though. The soul who would inhabit the body that you left behind would have the memories of a life that was not their own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-03T05:20:36-07:00","id":1536736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verlan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536285-age-alteration?p=1536574#post1536574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am interested by your suggestion in regards to Regeneration, though. I usually think of physical damage when thinking about Regeneration, so I had not considered how it might affect the aging process.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is aging, if not a physical damage more insidious and deep that simple losing of body part? If not simply Regeneration, it is definitely within the possibility of Patterning/Unraveling Practices which allows for deep and fundamental changes in the target of the spell - and aging, as we understand, a fundamental part of how many organisms work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verlan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536285-age-alteration?p=1536574#post1536574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea of applying the regenerative capabilities of certain animals to oneself through the use of magic, as you and another in the thread have suggested.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can also Weave/Pattern into your pattern the capabilities of stopping aging, or even reversing it. Even Sleeper scientists can now do that in animals (see <a href=\"https://time.com/6246864/reverse-aging-scientists-discover-milestone/\" target=\"_blank\">Scientist Discovers Aging Clock to Speed and Reverse Aging</a>), imagine what Awakened can do with power of Life Arcanum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-03T09:29:04-07:00","id":1536752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536285-age-alteration?p=1536736#post1536736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is aging, if not a physical damage more insidious and deep that simple losing of body part?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a bit of a crude approximation of what is theorized about the actual physical processes, never mind questions of whether or not this is a cosmology in which the physical might just be an expression of an underlying symbolic element in the Supernal. The latter would be the thing spells need to engage with, same as how the Matter Arcanum is more concerned with perceptual recognition of substances than atomic qualities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can also Weave/Pattern into your pattern the capabilities of stopping aging, or even reversing it. Even Sleeper scientists can now do that in animals (see <a href=\"https://time.com/6246864/reverse-aging-scientists-discover-milestone/\" target=\"_blank\">Scientist Discovers Aging Clock to Speed and Reverse Aging</a>), imagine what Awakened can do with power of Life Arcanum.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's wait and see if that's a thing they can do with mice that aged naturally, at least.<br /> <br /> Still, spells of the Life Arcanum don't really target things along the lines of molecular biochemistry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-03T13:01:47-07:00","id":1536760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536285-age-alteration?p=1536736#post1536736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is aging, if not a physical damage more insidious and deep that simple losing of body part? If not simply Regeneration, it is definitely within the possibility of Patterning/Unraveling Practices which allows for deep and fundamental changes in the target of the spell - and aging, as we understand, a fundamental part of how many organisms work.<br /> <br /> <br /> You can also Weave/Pattern into your pattern the capabilities of stopping aging, or even reversing it. Even Sleeper scientists can now do that in animals (see <a href=\"https://time.com/6246864/reverse-aging-scientists-discover-milestone/\" target=\"_blank\">Scientist Discovers Aging Clock to Speed and Reverse Aging</a>), imagine what Awakened can do with power of Life Arcanum.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was under the impression that the aging process was essentially hardwired into many living organisms. That being said, it seems like it would be possible to use Life magic to edit that. It would probably me more along the lines of transformation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-03T13:32:41-07:00","id":1536761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verlan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536285-age-alteration?p=1536760#post1536760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was under the impression that the aging process was essentially hardwired into many living organisms.</div> </div> </div> </div>That does not mean magic cannot change it. Indeed, change of fundamental, essential qualities of Patterns is definition of Patterning Practice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verlan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536285-age-alteration?p=1536760#post1536760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That being said, it seems like it would be possible to use Life magic to edit that. It would probably me more along the lines of transformation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yes. The only real question is: is it possible to make such spell Lasting? The answer is up to Storyteller, but, from my experience, it's better to allow clever usages of Practices and Arcana and try to work with consequences of having such power, instead of going &quot;nuh-uh, not possible!&quot;. There is lot of wonderful and absolutely <i>terrifying</i> applications of such power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}